<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  The protection loop. Replaces the reconcile loop (com.cuansniffer.reconcile),
  which this plist was derived from -- read the next paragraph, because what
  this process is allowed to do is NOT what that one was.

  Every PROTECT_POLL_SEC (60s), independent of the trader's 450s signal loop,
  it reads the venue and makes sure each open position carries exactly one
  reduce-only stop sized to the WHOLE position, replacing one that is missing,
  mis-sized or on the wrong side of the mark.

  WHAT IT CAN DO AT THE VENUE. It places reduce-only trigger orders, cancels
  them, and calls flatten_all -- which cancels every resting order and
  MARKET-CLOSES every position the venue holds. It does that when a position
  cannot be given a valid stop after two attempts, on the principle that an
  unprotected position is not the trade.

  So this process can close a position, including one opened by hand at the
  venue that it cannot find a stop price for. It cannot OPEN one: nothing it
  imports can size or enter a position, and a test asserts that. The plist
  this was derived from asserted the broader claim -- that it could place no
  order at all -- which was true of the reconcile loop and false of this one.

  There is deliberately no LEVELS_LIVE_ARMED. Protection must work whether or
  not the trader is armed -- a position with no stop is the one condition that
  is worse when nobody is trading, because nothing else is looking.

  It writes _trade_meta.json (the plan for a position it adopted) and
  _halt.json. It does NOT write _live_state.json; the trader stays that
  file's only writer.

  Install:
    cp deploy/launchd/com.cuansniffer.protect.plist ~/Library/LaunchAgents/
    launchctl load -w ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.cuansniffer.protect.plist
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>com.cuansniffer.protect</string>

  <!-- The venv's own python, NOT its resolved homebrew target. CPython only
       adds the venv's site-packages when invoked through the venv directory. -->
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/Users/myair/CuanSniffer/.venv/bin/python</string>
    <string>-u</string>
    <string>-m</string>
    <string>tools.protect_loop</string>
  </array>

  <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
  <string>/Users/myair/CuanSniffer</string>

  <!-- Deliberately NO LEVELS_LIVE_ARMED: protection must work whether or not
       the trader is armed. This does NOT make the process read-only -- see
       the header. It places stops and can market-close a position; what it
       cannot do is open one. -->

  <key>RunAtLoad</key>
  <true/>
  <key>KeepAlive</key>
  <true/>
  <key>ThrottleInterval</key>
  <integer>30</integer>

  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>/Users/myair/Library/Logs/cuan-sniffer/protect.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>/Users/myair/Library/Logs/cuan-sniffer/protect.err.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
